# BOC-(13C2-15N-2D2-glycine)-fluoride, 5-qubit NMR molecule
# Reference [16]: R. Marx et al., Phys. Rev. A 60, 2966 (1999) / similar fluorinated glycine
#
# Nuclei (5):
#   0 = F   (19F fluoride)
#   1 = C1  (13C alpha-carbon)
#   2 = C2  (13C carbonyl)
#   3 = N   (15N nitrogen)
#   4 = H   (amide 1H)
#
# W formulas (consistent with acetyl chloride derivation):
#   Two-qubit:    W(u,v) = round(10000 / (4 * J_Hz))
#   Single-qubit: W(u,u) = round(pi * 10000 / |min_shift_diff_Hz|)
#
# Approximate J-coupling values (Hz):
#   1J(F,C1)  ≈ 200  → W ≈ 13
#   1J(C1,C2) ≈  55  → W ≈ 45
#   1J(N,H)   ≈  90  → W ≈ 28
#   1J(C2,N)  ≈  10  → W ≈ 250
#   2J(F,C2)  ≈  20  → W ≈ 125
#   2J(C1,N)  ≈   5  → W ≈ 500
#   2J(C1,H)  ≈   5  → W ≈ 500
#   2J(C2,H)  ≈   7  → W ≈ 357
#   3J(F,N)   ≈   3  → W ≈ 833
#   4J(F,H)   ≈   2  → W ≈ 1250
#
# NOTE: values are approximate; exact coupling matrix from [16] required for
#       precise Table III reproduction.
5
# --- Single-qubit weights ---
single 0  5.0
single 1 20.0
single 2 20.0
single 3 30.0
single 4 10.0
# --- Two-qubit weights (sorted by W, fast to slow) ---
two 0 1   13.0
two 3 4   28.0
two 1 2   45.0
two 0 2  125.0
two 2 3  250.0
two 2 4  357.0
two 1 3  500.0
two 1 4  500.0
two 0 3  833.0
two 0 4 1250.0
